  "question": {
    "text": "The mole fraction of a solute in a binary solution is $0.1 .$ At $298 \\mathrm{~K}$, molarity of this solution is same as as its molality. Density of this solution at $298 \\mathrm{~K}$ is $2.0 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~cm}^{-3}$. The ratio of molecular weights of the solute and the solvent $\\left(\\mathrm{M}_{\\text {solute }} / \\mathrm{M}_{\\text {solvent }}\\right)$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "V1NVi",
      "text": "9",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6WPa8",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{9}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ce5Pk",
